.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-3.0-or-later
.Dd October 30, 2026
.Dt NQCARD 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nqcard ,
.Nm nqcardvrfy
.Nd make and check an identity card for a signing key
.Sh LIBRARY
libnoqtis, \-lnoqtis
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In noqtis.h
.Ft int
.Fo nqcard
.Fa "nqsalg alg" "const uint8_t *sk" "size_t sklen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *pk" "size_t pklen" "const char *name"
.Fa "const char *orcid" "const char *email" "const char *url"
.Fa "const char *affil" "int64_t created"
.Fa "char *out" "size_t cap" "size_t *outlen"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo nqcardvrfy
.Fa "const char *card" "size_t n" "const uint8_t *pk" "size_t pklen"
.Fa "nqcardf *f"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn nqcard
writes to
.Fa out ,
of
.Fa cap
bytes, an identity card
.Pq Ql noqtis-idcard-1 , Xr noqtis-capsule 5
in canonical JSON: the public key
.Fa pk
of
.Fa alg
with
.Fa name
and, when not
.Dv NULL ,
.Fa orcid ,
.Fa email ,
.Fa url
and
.Fa affil ,
made at
.Fa created
(seconds since 1970-01-01T00:00:00Z) and signed by
.Fa sk
under the context
.Ql noqtis-idcard-1 .
.Fa *outlen
gets the card's size, also when
.Fa cap
is too small.
The signature is verified before the card is written.
.Pp
In symbols, with B64 the padded base64 of RFC 4648 section 4, ALG the
algorithm's name as
.Xr nqsign 3
gives it, T the time as
.Ql YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ ,
and JCS the canonical JSON of RFC 8785 (members sorted by name, those
not given left out):
.Bd -literal -offset indent
body = JCS({"affil": affil, "alg": ALG, "created": T, "email": email,
            "format": "noqtis-idcard-1", "key": B64(pk), "name": name,
            "orcid": orcid, "url": url})
sig  = Sign(sk, body, "noqtis-idcard-1")     pure, hedged
card = JCS(body's members and "signature": B64(sig))
.Ed
.Pp
where Sign is
.Xr nqsign 3
with the context
.Ql noqtis-idcard-1
(15 bytes) and
.Fa ph
0.
.Pp
The fields, in bytes:
.Fa name
and
.Fa affil
are 1 to 255 bytes of UTF-8 with no control character (C0, DEL or C1)
and no space at either end;
.Fa orcid
is an ORCID iD,
.Ql 0000-0002-1825-0097 ,
or its
.Ql https://orcid.org/ ,
.Ql http://orcid.org/ ,
.Ql https://www.orcid.org/
or
.Ql http://www.orcid.org/
address, whose last character is its ISO 7064 MOD 11-2 check digit
.Pq Ql X No for 10 ,
a lower-case
.Ql x
taken as
.Ql X ;
the card holds the bare iD.
.Fa email
is
.Ql local@domain.tld ,
at most
.Dv NQCARDEMAIL
(254) bytes;
.Fa url
an
.Ql https://
address with a host, at most
.Dv NQCARDURL
(1024) bytes; neither has a space or a control character.
The arguments and fields are checked before the algorithm, so a call
refused for a field returns
.Er NQEARG
whatever
.Fa alg
is.
.Pp
.Fn nqcardvrfy
checks the
.Fa n
bytes at
.Fa card
(at most
.Dv NQCARDMAX ,
256 KiB): it must be a
.Ql noqtis-idcard-1
card in canonical form, with exactly its members, fields within the
limits above (the ORCID iD bare, its check digit right), a post-quantum
algorithm, a key and a signature of that algorithm's sizes, and a
signature that verifies under the key it carries with the context
.Ql noqtis-idcard-1 .
With
.Fa pk
not
.Dv NULL ,
the card's key must also be
.Fa pk ,
of
.Fa pklen
bytes.
On success
.Fa *f
gets the card:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
typedef struct {
  nqsalg alg;
  uint8_t pk[NQCARDPK];   /* the card's public key, pklen bytes */
  size_t pklen;
  uint8_t fp[32];         /* its SHA-256 (nqinsp's info.key) */
  int64_t created;        /* seconds since 1970, UTC */
  char utc[21];           /* the same, YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ */
  char name[256];
  char orcid[20];         /* "" for a field the card has not */
  char email[NQCARDEMAIL + 1];
  char url[NQCARDURL + 1];
  char affil[256];
} nqcardf;
.Ed
.Pp
On any other result
.Fa *f
is zeroed.
A card is self-signed: a card that verifies was written by whoever holds
its key and is unchanged, which does not make the name true; compare
.Fa fp
with the one its holder published, or pin
.Fa pk .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Bl -tag -width NQENOSUP
.It Dv NQOK
The card was written, or it verifies.
.It Bq Er NQEBUF
.Fa cap
is too small.
.It Bq Er NQENOSUP
.Fn nqcard :
the algorithm is not a post-quantum signature (Ed25519 alone) or is not
a signature algorithm of noqtis.
.It Bq Er NQEARG
A
.Dv NULL
argument, a field out of its limits, keys of the wrong sizes or not a
pair, or
.Fa created
before 1970 or after 9999.
.It Bq Er NQEVRFY
.Fn nqcardvrfy :
the signature does not verify, or the card is not for
.Fa pk .
.It Bq Er NQEDEC
.Fn nqcardvrfy :
not a card as above.
.It Bq Er NQELIM
.Fn nqcardvrfy :
more than
.Dv NQCARDMAX
bytes.
.It Bq Er NQEMEM
The allocation hook returned
.Dv NULL .
.It Bq Er NQERNG , NQEFLT
.Fn nqcard :
as
.Xr nqsign 3 .
.El
.Pp
.Fn nqcardvrfy
also returns
.Er NQEARG
for a
.Dv NULL
.Fa card
or
.Fa f ,
or a
.Dv NULL
.Fa pk
with
.Fa pklen
not 0.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Make a card for an ML-DSA-65 key pair and read it back, pinned to the
key:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
static char card[16384];
nqcardf f;
size_t n;
int rc = nqcard(NQMLDSA65, sk, sklen, pk, pklen, "A. Researcher",
                "0000-0002-1825-0097", NULL, NULL, NULL,
                (int64_t)time(NULL), card, sizeof card, &n);
if (rc == NQOK)
  rc = nqcardvrfy(card, n, pk, pklen, &f);
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis-check 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-idcard 1 ,
.Xr nqinsp 3 ,
.Xr nqkstmt 3 ,
.Xr noqtis-capsule 5
